From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:16:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/27] NEXUS engine: shader and pipeline status for the NEXUS
 performance interface

nexus_shader_status.h reads, per session, how the pipelines a game used
got ready (built from the disk cache at boot, by the background prebuild,
or compiled when first used) and the shader job scheduler's builds queued,
running and failed. The pipeline cache registers its scheduler there.
StutterTrace's first-use lookup counters now always run (one relaxed
atomic add per pipeline) instead of only with EDEN_NX2_STUTTER_TRACE.
nexus_engine reports them as "shaders" in its status while a session runs.

